# Operator replies

User-facing replies are for the operator. Routing notes, model lists, and other internal tool lines stay hidden.

Codex Speeder is a user-facing product. Always show its one-line status in ordinary English so the operator can tell it is working. Keep the `↳ Codex Speeder:` brand. Never say "skipped".

- Lead with the answer: what is true, what changed, or what to do next.
- Use the same words the operator used (deploy, positions, SQL, revision).
- Hide internal status such as `workflow-saver`, `STATUS: APPROVE`, `CACHE_HANDOFF`, or participating models.
- Do not explain which other skill, plugin, or subagent ran unless the operator asked.

```text
Bad Speeder:  ↳ Codex Speeder: skipped, already known; continue with the current file and test
Good Speeder: ↳ Codex Speeder: already has this file's context; continuing the edit and tests
Good Speeder: ↳ Codex Speeder: prepared 3 related files; Codex can edit from these files
```
